=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  status hardened ----------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Debian 13 after hardn: alice in sudo, ufw allowing 2230 alone,$
# sshd on 2230 refusing root's login and passwords, AppArmor$
# enforcing, unattended-upgrades on, hardn.yml's nameservers in$
# use; up 3 days.$
$
hardn  v0.4.0              https://github.com/abbott/hardn$
$
# Debian 13 (Trixie) ###########################################$
$
  [web-01]                 192.0.2.20$
                           3 days, 5 hours, 12 minutes$
$
  [*] Risk Level           Minimal ~ hardened security$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [+] SSH Port             Configured non-default (2230)$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
  [+] DNS                  Configured 192.0.2.54, 2001:db8::54$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured unattended-upgrades$
  [+] AppArmor             Configured 7 profiles enforced$
$
----------------------------------------------------------------$
$
  Select an option         Mode Live$
$
   1) User Management      Create, configure (sudo, SSH keys)$
   2) SSH Login            Root login, passwords, port$
   3) Firewall             Configure ufw rules$
   4) DNS                  Configure nameservers$
   6) Run All              Execute hardening operations$
   7) Backup               Configure hardn backup$
   8) Configuration        View hardn.yml$
   9) System Details       View system information$
  10) Logs                 View log file$
$
   0) Exit                 q to quit$
$
    > Option [0-4, 6-10 or q]:$
$
$

